/-!
# Synchronizing neighboring level joins on a retained hair

Independently selected controlled joins need not initially end at the same
point of their common retained access hair.  Following Moise 9.6, choose the
shallower of the two points.  Exactly one join then needs a nondegenerate
extension along the hair, and that extension meets the boundary-side hair
segment only at the synchronized point.
-/

